findings.problem:
Three different things use icon('camera'), a compact-camera glyph with a lens and flash bump:
- the action-bar button (C, src/ui/screens.ts:55), which resets the orbit;
- the pause tile 'View: Standard' (screens.ts:159), which cycles the lens;
- the controls-map row 'mouse / C / camera / RS' (screens.ts:169).

New players read a camera icon on an action bar as 'take a photo'. Only the aria-label says 'Reset camera'. The pause map row draws mouse + C → camera icon, which suggests that the mouse and C both do the same 'camera' thing. In fact right-drag orbits, the wheel zooms and C resets. The reset itself works well: after an orbit plus zoom, C restores the exact home view (shots 53 → 54), and from the survey too (shot 56). But the player can't tell from the icon that this is what it does.
